WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.028
Imagine three friends sharing a bag of thirty sweets equally. Each friend gets ten. Sharing a total out equally is exactly what an average does.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:19.258
In Business, the average is called the mean. The mean equals the total divided by the number of items, such as shops, showrooms or units.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:32.214
Here is a business example. Four cafés sell twelve hundred, eighteen hundred, fourteen hundred and sixteen hundred cups. The total is six thousand. Six thousand divided by four is fifteen hundred cups per café.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:45.871
The method has three steps. Find the total being shared out. Find the number of outlets or units. Then divide the total by the number, and write the unit.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:58.628
Write large numbers in full before you divide. Nine million is nine followed by six zeros. Two point five million is two million, five hundred thousand. A billion has nine zeros.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:08.136
Exam cases often give extra figures, such as employees or turnover. Use only the total and the count the question asks about.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:20.887
Here is a real question from Paper two in June twenty nineteen. Calculate the average number of vehicles sold in each car showroom. It is worth two marks.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:30.716
The case gives four figures. We need vehicles sold, nine million, and showrooms, six thousand. The employees and the turnover are not needed.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:38.757
Write nine million in full, then divide by six thousand. Nine million divided by six thousand is fifteen hundred vehicles per showroom.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:49.895
A common mistake is using the wrong figure, such as the employees. That gives ten, which is employees per showroom, not vehicles.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:58.727
Another mistake is dividing the wrong way round. A tiny answer like this is a warning sign. The total always goes on top.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:17.281
Now you try. A bakery chain sells two point four million loaves a year through three hundred shops. It employs eighteen hundred staff. Calculate the average number of loaves sold per shop. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:30.836
Two point four million is two million, four hundred thousand. Ignore the staff. Divide by three hundred shops. The answer is eight thousand loaves per shop.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:40.088
Remember the method: find the total, find the number, then divide and write the unit. Now try the practice questions for this type.
